[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
To start VDR at boot:

  # sysrc vdr_enable=YES

Plugins and other command line options go into vdr_flags, e.g.:

  # sysrc vdr_flags="-Pskincurses"

See %%PREFIX%%/etc/rc.d/vdr for the other rc.conf variables.

Recordings are stored in %%VIDEODIR%%. The rc script creates this
directory on first start if it does not exist.

DVB devices are provided by multimedia/webcamd. VDR starts as root and
then drops its privileges to the "%%VDR_USER%%" user, which needs access
to the DVB device nodes:

  # pw groupmod webcamd -m %%VDR_USER%%

As VDR does not run as root:
- it cannot set the system clock from the broadcast time
  (Setup > EPG > "Set system time"), use ntpd(8) instead.
- it does not write core dumps unless kern.sugid_coredump=1 is set.
EOM
}
]
